1052
00:49:16.130 --> 00:49:18.970
She confronts Dwight, and he blows her off again.
她去找德怀特对质，而他又一次把她打发走了。

1053
00:49:19.330 --> 00:49:20.910
Yeah, so she's bummed out.
对，所以她挺沮丧的。

1054
00:49:21.070 --> 00:49:24.490
She's sitting by herself on some, I guess they were straw bales.
她一个人坐在一些，我猜应该是草包的东西上。

1055
00:49:24.630 --> 00:49:24.890
Yeah.
对。

1056
00:49:25.250 --> 00:49:27.830
A nice man is going to walk up.
一个好心的人会走过来。

1057
00:49:28.190 --> 00:49:28.670
Yeah.
对。

1058
00:49:28.890 --> 00:49:31.270
He's going to say, do you mind if we share this bale?
他会说，介意我们共用这个草包吗？

1059
00:49:31.590 --> 00:49:31.950
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1060
00:49:31.950 --> 00:49:35.450
And she says, sure, there's no charge to sit on the hay, is there?
然后她说，当然不介意，坐在干草上不用收费吧？

1061
00:49:35.790 --> 00:49:41.550
Yes, and that man is a major guest star in the house.
没错，而且那个男人是《豪斯医生》里的主要客串明星。

1062
00:49:41.830 --> 00:49:42.230
What?
什么？

1063
00:49:42.450 --> 00:49:42.870
Oh, no.
哦，不会吧。

1064
00:49:43.010 --> 00:49:44.030
Was he also in house?
他也演过《豪斯医生》？

1065
00:49:44.130 --> 00:49:45.730
He was in house.
他演过《豪斯医生》。

1066
00:49:46.230 --> 00:49:48.150
This is Jack Coleman.
这就是杰克·科尔曼。

1067
00:49:48.150 --> 00:50:04.730
And lady, I got the most wonderful tweet from a fan of our podcast, The Filthy Ape, sent us a link to every crossover between The Office and House.
天哪，我们播客《肮脏的猿猴》的一位粉丝给我发了一条超级棒的推文，给我们发了一个链接，里面包含了《办公室》和《豪斯医生》所有的交叉客串。

1068
00:50:05.010 --> 00:50:05.870
Come on.
真的假的？

1069
00:50:06.110 --> 00:50:10.390
There were 148 cast and crew members.
一共有148名演员和剧组工作人员。

1070
00:50:10.510 --> 00:50:11.710
How happy are you right now?
你现在有多开心？

1071
00:50:11.710 --> 00:50:17.390
Who worked on both The Office and House, and Jack Coleman is one of them.
他们既参与过《办公室》又参与过《豪斯医生》，杰克·科尔曼就是其中之一。

1072
00:50:18.150 --> 00:50:25.090
I had just watched the show Heroes, and so when he got cast to play the senator, I was like, oh, no, he's a scary guy on Heroes.
我当时刚看完《英雄》这部剧，所以当他被选来演参议员时，我就想，噢，不，他在《英雄》里是个吓人的家伙。

1073
00:50:25.430 --> 00:50:26.730
He plays a lot of villains.
他演过很多反派。

1074
00:50:26.730 --> 00:50:37.070
He was also a villain on Castle, but he is very well known for also playing the role of Stephen Carrington in the 1980s primetime soap opera Dynasty.
他也在《灵书妙探》里演过反派，但他最为人熟知的角色之一，还是20世纪80年代黄金档肥皂剧《豪门恩怨》里的斯蒂芬·卡灵顿。

1075
00:50:37.910 --> 00:50:39.710
Jack is a delight to hang around.
跟杰克在一起相处非常开心。

1076
00:50:39.710 --> 00:50:42.550
He has so many good stories, and he's so nice.
他有好多精彩的故事，人也非常好。

1077
00:50:42.690 --> 00:50:47.210
Well, according to Wikipedia, he's a sixth-generation descendant of Benjamin Franklin.
嗯，根据维基百科记载，他是本杰明·富兰克林的第六代直系后代。

1078
00:50:47.430 --> 00:50:47.710
What?
什么？

1079
00:50:48.150 --> 00:50:48.450
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1080
00:50:48.950 --> 00:50:49.970
It's true.
真的。

1081
00:50:50.310 --> 00:50:51.390
It's on Wikipedia.
维基百科上写着呢。

1082
00:50:52.110 --> 00:50:59.790
But then another guest star alert, the little boy, who's with the senator, was played by Griffin Gluck.
还有另一个客串明星提醒，和参议员在一起的小男孩是由格里芬·格鲁克饰演的。

1083
00:50:59.930 --> 00:51:02.850
And we got a fan catch from Jessica S.
我们收到了来自加拿大艾伯塔省云杉林镇的杰西卡·S.发来的粉丝爆料，她说，

1084
00:51:03.070 --> 00:51:05.910
from Spruce Grove, Alberta, Canada, who said,
来自加拿大艾伯塔省云杉林镇的杰西卡·S.说，

1085
00:51:06.290 --> 00:51:14.350
I spotted Griffin Gluck, who went on to find success in many TV series and movies, including Tall Girl with Angela Kinsey.
我认出了格里芬·格鲁克，他后来在许多电视剧和电影中都取得了成功，包括与安吉拉·金西合作的《高个女孩》。

1086
00:51:15.350 --> 00:51:15.790
Yes.
对。

1087
00:51:16.430 --> 00:51:17.750
So listen to this.
所以听我说这个。

1088
00:51:18.350 --> 00:51:19.790
Tall Girl is so much fun.
《高个女孩》太有趣了。

1089
00:51:19.910 --> 00:51:21.370
You know, it's a movie I did for Netflix.
你知道，那是我为网飞拍的一部电影。

1090
00:51:21.610 --> 00:51:22.650
I play dorky mom.
我演一个书呆子妈妈。

1091
00:51:23.030 --> 00:51:24.990
Steve Zahn and I are like the dorky parents.
史蒂夫·扎恩和我饰演那对有点书呆子气的父母。

1092
00:51:25.290 --> 00:51:26.690
Our daughter's very tall.
我们女儿个子很高。

1093
00:51:26.690 --> 00:51:31.970
But there's this sweet boy that has a crush on her in the movie, played by Griffin Gluck.
但电影里有个可爱的男孩暗恋她，由格里芬·格鲁克饰演。

1094
00:51:32.090 --> 00:51:34.150
The character's name is Jack Dunkelman.
这个角色的名字叫杰克·邓克尔曼。

1095
00:51:34.710 --> 00:51:37.190
Griffin is so good in this movie.
格里芬在这部电影里表现得太棒了。

1096
00:51:37.450 --> 00:51:40.870
And in the first movie, we didn't really have any scenes together.
在第一部电影里，我们其实没有什么对手戏。

1097
00:51:40.870 --> 00:51:48.710
But we crossed paths just once, and we were hanging out and talking, and he said, we've actually met before.
但我们偶遇过一次，当时我们在一起闲聊，他说，我们其实以前见过。

1098
00:51:48.910 --> 00:51:50.250
And I was like, when?
然后我就问，什么时候？

1099
00:51:50.570 --> 00:51:53.030
And he said, well, it's just a brief moment.
他说，哦，那只是个短暂的瞬间。

1100
00:51:53.030 --> 00:51:56.850
You probably don't remember, but I was the senator's son in Hay Place.
你可能不记得了，但我就是在《干草广场》里演参议员儿子的那个小孩。

1101
00:51:56.850 --> 00:52:04.450
And I was like, oh, I remember they gave him this huge candied apple that he had to try to eat.
然后我就说，哦，我想起来了，他们给了他一个巨大的糖苹果，他得努力把它吃完。

1102
00:52:04.530 --> 00:52:05.410
It was like massive.
那苹果简直巨大无比。

1103
00:52:05.910 --> 00:52:09.810
And I was like, I cannot believe, Griffin, that you were in Hay Place.
当时我就想，格里芬，真不敢相信你竟然去过稻草乐园。

1104
00:52:10.410 --> 00:52:14.850
But his performance is so good in Tall Girl and Tall Girl, too, if you guys haven't seen it.
但他俩在《高个女生》和《高个女生2》里的表现都太棒了，如果你们还没看过的话。

1105
00:52:15.230 --> 00:52:16.910
Well, I'm sure he must have looked so different.
嗯，我敢肯定他肯定变样了。

1106
00:52:16.930 --> 00:52:17.930
I mean, he had grown.
我是说，他长大了。

1107
00:52:18.270 --> 00:52:18.630
Yes.
对。

1108
00:52:18.730 --> 00:52:19.610
I mean, yes.
我是说，对的。

1109
00:52:19.950 --> 00:52:21.150
It had been so long.
已经过去好久了。

1110
00:52:21.230 --> 00:52:22.150
Like, I felt old.
就感觉自己老了。

1111
00:52:22.290 --> 00:52:22.950
Do you know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

1112
00:52:22.950 --> 00:52:24.610
I was like, oh, right.
我就想，哦，对。

1113
00:52:25.670 --> 00:52:27.350
But he's a great actor.
但他是个好演员。

1114
00:52:27.750 --> 00:52:31.710
Now, you said something just now, Angela, where you said he played the senator's son.
安吉拉，你刚才说他演的是参议员的儿子，对吧？

1115
00:52:32.630 --> 00:52:32.990
Yes.
对。

1116
00:52:33.690 --> 00:52:34.830
Fan mail flurry.
粉丝来信如雪花般飞来。

1117
00:52:35.610 --> 00:52:40.910
Lots of people want to know, hey, what happened to the senator's son?
好多人都想知道，嘿，参议员的儿子怎么了？

1118
00:52:41.070 --> 00:52:42.090
Um, guess what?
呃，你猜怎么着？

1119
00:52:42.090 --> 00:52:44.950
I would say this every year on the show.
我在节目里每年都要说这个。

1120
00:52:46.090 --> 00:52:49.030
Because later, there's no son.
因为后来，就再也没有这个儿子了。

1121
00:52:49.490 --> 00:52:50.050
Never.
从来没有。

1122
00:52:50.530 --> 00:52:52.990
I think I've solved that mystery.
我想我已经解开这个谜团了。

1123
00:52:53.290 --> 00:52:57.750
Well, I had my own character idea that I would talk to the writers about.
其实，我曾向编剧们提出过我自己的角色构想。

1124
00:52:57.870 --> 00:52:59.710
Because it was a joke between me and the writers.
因为这是我和编剧之间的玩笑。

1125
00:53:00.130 --> 00:53:03.210
At one point, we had a new writer that came on at the end of the series.
有一次，剧集快结束时来了一位新编剧。

1126
00:53:03.210 --> 00:53:07.150
And I'm going blank, like, on who all was in this conversation.
我记不清当时都有谁参与了这段对话。

1127
00:53:07.350 --> 00:53:11.650
But I remember them saying something about Angela and the senator having a baby.
但我记得他们提到过安吉拉和参议员有个孩子的事。

1128
00:53:11.770 --> 00:53:13.330
And I was like, well, you know, he's already a dad.
然后我就说，好吧，你知道的，他已经是个爸爸了。

1129
00:53:13.530 --> 00:53:15.290
And one of the new writers was like, what?
其中一个新编剧就问，什么？

1130
00:53:15.410 --> 00:53:17.310
And I'm like, yes, he had a son.
我说，对啊，他有个儿子。

1131
00:53:17.870 --> 00:53:18.510
Evan T.
来自华盛顿州布雷默顿的埃文·T.

1132
00:53:18.930 --> 00:53:22.970
from Bremerton, Washington, thinks he didn't have a son.
认为他根本没有儿子。

1133
00:53:22.970 --> 00:53:27.590
Oh, Evan, this is very different than my backstory that I created.
哦，埃文，这和我自己编的故事背景可太不一样了。

1134
00:53:28.090 --> 00:53:33.810
Evan says, if you watch the scene, the senator never says the boy is his son.
埃文说，如果你看那个场景，参议员从来没说过那是他的亲生儿子。

1135
00:53:34.230 --> 00:53:35.750
It could be his nephew.
那可能是他侄子。

1136
00:53:36.170 --> 00:53:38.650
It could be child of a friend.
也可能是朋友的孩子。

1137
00:53:39.430 --> 00:53:40.630
Let's take a listen.
我们来听听看。

1138
00:53:41.810 --> 00:53:43.610
Do you mind if we share this bail?
你介意我们共用一捆稻草吗？

1139
00:53:44.250 --> 00:53:44.850
Sure.
当然不介意。

1140
00:53:45.790 --> 00:53:47.950
There's no charge to sit on the hay, is there?
坐在稻草上应该不收费吧？

1141
00:53:48.390 --> 00:53:48.750
Probably.
可能会收吧。

1142
00:53:50.050 --> 00:53:55.150
Wouldn't you think the $10 to build your own broom would include the hay and not just the instructions?
你不觉得花10美元自己做一把扫帚应该包含稻草，而不只是说明书吗？

1143
00:53:55.430 --> 00:53:58.150
I mean, I'm starting to think this guy is just trying to make money off the holiday.
我是说，我开始觉得这家伙就是在借节日发财。

1144
00:53:58.590 --> 00:54:00.890
Yeah, instead of hay place, it should be pay place.
对啊，与其叫稻草乐园（Hay Place），不如叫付费乐园（Pay Place）。

1145
00:54:01.950 --> 00:54:02.930
Don't laugh at me.
别笑话我。

1146
00:54:03.110 --> 00:54:03.970
No, no, no, I wasn't.
不不不，我没有。

1147
00:54:04.090 --> 00:54:05.630
I was just laughing at your joke.
我只是在笑你的梗。

1148
00:54:06.530 --> 00:54:06.890
No.
才不是。

1149
00:54:09.700 --> 00:54:10.420
Pay place.
付费乐园。

1150
00:54:11.400 --> 00:54:14.460
Yeah, so we can celebrate Thanksgiving me your money day.
对啊，这样我们就能庆祝感恩节“把钱交出来日”了。

1151
00:54:15.840 --> 00:54:16.740
That's humorous.
真幽默。

1152
00:54:17.040 --> 00:54:17.660
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1153
00:54:18.900 --> 00:54:19.600
That's it.
就这样。

1154
00:54:20.760 --> 00:54:23.280
Doesn't say, can my son and I have a seat?
没写，我和我儿子能坐这儿吗？

1155
00:54:23.600 --> 00:54:23.940
Right.
对。

1156
00:54:25.200 --> 00:54:26.460
No, you're right, Evan.
不，你说得对，埃文。

1157
00:54:26.820 --> 00:54:31.880
My theory that I used to say was, as soon as the senator and Angela got married, she sent him away.
我以前提出的理论是，参议员和安吉拉一结婚，她就把他打发走了。

1158
00:54:32.160 --> 00:54:33.780
Like to military school or something?
比如送去军事学校什么的？

1159
00:54:33.800 --> 00:54:35.100
Yeah, like some kind of boarding school.
对，就像某种寄宿学校。

1160
00:54:35.940 --> 00:54:39.440
Well, if it was his son, I believe that's exactly what happened.
好吧，如果那是他的儿子，我相信事情确实就是这样的。

1161
00:54:39.820 --> 00:54:42.620
But I was intrigued by Evan's theory.
但我对埃文的理论很感兴趣。

1162
00:54:42.620 --> 00:54:46.360
Evan will have to keep clocking that as the episodes progress with the senator.
随着剧集的发展，埃文得继续关注参议员的动向。

1163
00:54:46.620 --> 00:54:48.520
We've all just made an assumption.
我们都只是做了一个假设。

1164
00:54:48.860 --> 00:54:49.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1165
00:54:49.780 --> 00:54:55.120
We should also point out before we leave hay place that Kevin has just entered the maze.
在我们离开干草农场之前，我们还得指出凯文刚刚进入了迷宫。

1166
00:54:55.460 --> 00:54:55.840
Yeah.
对。

1167
00:54:56.320 --> 00:54:57.480
It's not going to go well.
这不会顺利的。

1168
00:54:57.620 --> 00:54:58.280
It's not.
确实不会。

1169
00:54:58.680 --> 00:55:00.840
We have some malaise in the break room.
休息室里有些沉闷压抑。

1170
00:55:01.700 --> 00:55:03.220
Malaise in the break room?
休息室里压抑？

1171
00:55:03.420 --> 00:55:03.660
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1172
00:55:03.900 --> 00:55:04.900
I love it.
我喜欢。

1173
00:55:04.900 --> 00:55:12.960
And, yeah, Michael is sorting the trash, and Pam is going to have to have, like, an intervention, I guess.
然后，对，迈克尔在分类垃圾，而帕姆大概不得不进行某种干预。

1174
00:55:13.600 --> 00:55:21.580
She's doing the Pam thing that Pam does with Michael, where she's the voice of reason and sort of holds up a mirror to what's really happening,
她做着帕姆对迈克尔时常做的那种事，扮演着理性的声音，某种程度上像照镜子一样映照出真实发生的事情，

1175
00:55:21.580 --> 00:55:24.820
and that's usually the only time he can see it.
而那通常是他唯一能看清的时候。

1176
00:55:24.820 --> 00:55:28.900
And he's going to say, you may be right, I may be crazy.
而且他会说，你说得对，我可能疯了。

1177
00:55:29.360 --> 00:55:30.300
About Ryan.
关于瑞恩。

1178
00:55:30.640 --> 00:55:30.880
Yeah.
对。

1179
00:55:31.580 --> 00:55:34.860
Which means Pam knows he wants to break into song.
这意味着帕姆知道他想放声歌唱。

1180
00:55:35.140 --> 00:55:35.440
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1181
00:55:36.300 --> 00:55:40.760
Randy said that we had to pay $25,000.
兰迪说我们得付两万五千美元。

1182
00:55:41.140 --> 00:55:43.080
Oh, just for that little moment?
哦，就为了那一小会儿？

1183
00:55:43.140 --> 00:55:46.440
For Steve to sing that one line of the Billy Joel song.
就为了让史蒂夫唱比利·乔尔的那首歌的一句歌词。

1184
00:55:46.860 --> 00:55:47.420
Whoa!
哇！

1185
00:55:48.020 --> 00:55:48.420
Yeah.
对。

1186
00:55:48.640 --> 00:55:50.140
What if we sang the whole song?
如果我们把整首歌都唱了会怎样？

1187
00:55:50.460 --> 00:55:51.540
I don't know.
我不知道。

1188
00:55:51.820 --> 00:55:52.940
Is it, like, per line?
是按行收费的吗？

1189
00:55:53.520 --> 00:55:54.760
That's a good question.
是个好问题。

1190
00:55:55.120 --> 00:55:55.380
Wow.
哇。

1191
00:55:55.380 --> 00:55:56.480
I'll get to the bottom of that.
我会弄清楚这件事的。

1192
00:55:57.020 --> 00:56:01.620
After this talk with Pam, Michael's going to go find Ryan in his closet office.
在和帕姆谈过之后，迈克尔去找他杂物间办公室里的瑞恩。

1193
00:56:02.060 --> 00:56:03.640
This scene broke my heart.
这一幕让我心碎。

1194
00:56:03.860 --> 00:56:04.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1195
00:56:04.460 --> 00:56:11.520
Before we discuss it, at 15 minutes, 30 seconds, when Michael opens the door, did you see what was on Ryan's screen?
在我们讨论之前，在15分30秒时，迈克尔打开门，你看到瑞恩屏幕上是什么了吗？

1196
00:56:11.640 --> 00:56:12.500
Some sort of game.
某种游戏。

1197
00:56:12.700 --> 00:56:13.640
Like a baseball game.
就像棒球游戏。

1198
00:56:14.000 --> 00:56:16.100
And he quickly changes it to Wolf.com.
而他迅速切换到了Wolf.com。

1199
00:56:16.220 --> 00:56:17.460
But it was like a video game.
但那就像是个电子游戏。

1200
00:56:17.800 --> 00:56:18.200
Yeah.
对。

1201
00:56:18.380 --> 00:56:20.940
But he quickly changes it to look like he's busy.
但他迅速切换，好让自己看起来很忙。

1202
00:56:20.940 --> 00:56:21.480
Exactly.
没错。

1203
00:56:22.180 --> 00:56:22.620
Yeah.
对。

1204
00:56:22.740 --> 00:56:27.880
It's really sad because it's very clear that Ryan does not have Michael's best interest at heart.
这真的很让人难过，因为很明显瑞安根本没有把迈克尔的利益放在心上。

1205
00:56:28.320 --> 00:56:28.760
No.
没有。

1206
00:56:29.160 --> 00:56:32.400
And he wants Michael to take out a second mortgage on his condo.
而且他还想让迈克尔把他的公寓二次抵押贷款。

1207
00:56:33.020 --> 00:56:35.380
And Ryan says, we're going to do so much together.
瑞安还说，我们要一起做很多事。

1208
00:56:35.540 --> 00:56:36.700
We're going to have trips and dinners.
我们要一起去旅游、吃晚餐。

1209
00:56:36.800 --> 00:56:38.700
And Michael's like, well, we've never even had a dinner.
迈克尔就说，我们俩甚至连一次晚餐都没吃过呢。

1210
00:56:38.820 --> 00:56:39.380
How about tonight?
今晚怎么样？

1211
00:56:39.520 --> 00:56:40.740
And Ryan's like, yeah, I'm busy.
瑞安却说，行吧，我很忙。

1212
00:56:41.360 --> 00:56:41.640
Yeah.
是啊。

1213
00:56:42.160 --> 00:56:44.880
Well, Daryl is going to be less subtle.
嗯，达里尔就没那么委婉了。

1214
00:56:45.280 --> 00:56:45.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1215
00:56:45.720 --> 00:56:48.700
Daryl is going to literally remove.
达里尔会直接把人弄走。

1216
00:56:48.700 --> 00:56:48.940
Yank him.
把他拽走。

1217
00:56:49.500 --> 00:56:49.740
Yeah.
对。

1218
00:56:50.140 --> 00:56:50.960
Buy his shirt.
买下他的衬衫。

1219
00:56:52.300 --> 00:56:55.420
And everyone is going to really put the pressure on.
然后所有人都会真正施加压力。

1220
00:56:55.520 --> 00:56:56.140
They're in the kitchen.
他们在厨房里。

1221
00:56:56.140 --> 00:56:58.260
And they're all saying they want to sell.
他们都在说他们想卖掉。

1222
00:56:58.920 --> 00:57:01.520
Except Michael still doesn't want to sell.
只有迈克尔还是不想卖。

1223
00:57:01.760 --> 00:57:03.580
He still gets Ryan's back.
他依然护着瑞安。

1224
00:57:04.000 --> 00:57:09.940
By the way, something we forgot to mention was why Washington University wants to buy Wolf.
顺便说一句，我们忘了一个事没提，那就是为什么华盛顿大学想买下沃尔夫。

1225
00:57:10.760 --> 00:57:12.760
Oh, well, this is pretty important.
哦，这个其实挺重要的。

1226
00:57:13.000 --> 00:57:15.280
They realize it's just for the domain name.
他们意识到这只是为了域名。

1227
00:57:15.280 --> 00:57:17.820
It's the Washington University Public Health Fund.
那是华盛顿大学公共卫生基金会。

1228
00:57:18.060 --> 00:57:18.420
Yeah.
对。

1229
00:57:18.580 --> 00:57:21.640
And that should really show you how much this business is suffering.
这真的能说明这家公司的生意有多惨淡。

1230
00:57:22.080 --> 00:57:25.760
That just someone wanting to buy the domain name back.
仅仅是有人想把域名买回去。

1231
00:57:25.960 --> 00:57:26.360
Right.
没错。

1232
00:57:26.620 --> 00:57:28.700
Is enough to get out.
就足以让人脱手了。

1233
00:57:29.140 --> 00:57:33.720
Well, while this is going on, Jim has decided to spend the rest of his day
好吧，就在这期间，吉姆决定花剩下的时间

1234
00:57:34.820 --> 00:57:38.460
manipulating the audiobook of Joe Bennett's book.
恶搞乔·贝内特的有声书。

1235
00:57:39.500 --> 00:57:40.060
Yes.
对。

1236
00:57:40.580 --> 00:57:41.140
Yes.
对。

1237
00:57:41.360 --> 00:57:43.340
Basically pranking Gabe.
基本上就是在捉弄盖布。

1238
00:57:43.800 --> 00:57:44.060
Yeah.
对。

1239
00:57:44.500 --> 00:57:52.840
So he manipulates this message that sounds like Joe telling Gabe that she's going to read her audiobook to him
所以他剪辑了一段留言，听起来像是乔告诉盖布她要亲自把有声书读给他听

1240
00:57:52.840 --> 00:57:56.880
and he has to follow along to make sure she doesn't make any mistakes.
而且他必须跟着一起看，以确保她没有读错任何地方。

1241
00:57:57.200 --> 00:57:59.300
Do you know what I thought Jim was going to do?
你知道我以为吉姆要做什么吗？

1242
00:57:59.480 --> 00:57:59.880
What?
做什么？

1243
00:58:00.180 --> 00:58:06.620
I thought he was going to edit the audiobook to say, let Jim have his commissions back.
我以为他会把有声书剪辑成：把吉姆的佣金还给他。

1244
00:58:07.420 --> 00:58:07.980
Oh.
哦。

1245
00:58:08.920 --> 00:58:10.180
That would have been good.
那倒挺不错的。

1246
00:58:11.380 --> 00:58:14.160
We did have a fan catch from Louisa L.
我们确实收到了来自马萨诸塞州的粉丝

1247
00:58:14.380 --> 00:58:15.780
in Massachusetts who said,
路易莎·L.的纠错，她说，

1248
00:58:16.660 --> 00:58:20.600
wouldn't Jim's extension number have come up and not Joe's?
难道显示的不会是吉姆的分机号而不是乔的吗？

1249
00:58:21.160 --> 00:58:23.720
When like, quote unquote, Joe calls Gabe.
当也就是所谓乔给盖布打电话的时候。

1250
00:58:24.060 --> 00:58:24.800
So busted.
太穿帮了。

1251
00:58:25.120 --> 00:58:25.720
I know.
我也觉得。

1252
00:58:26.020 --> 00:58:27.240
Gabe was not paying attention.
盖布根本没注意。

1253
00:58:28.140 --> 00:58:31.660
Dwight is now going to crown himself the Hay King.
德怀特现在要给自己加冕为干草之王了。

1254
00:58:32.640 --> 00:58:33.200
Yes.
是的。

1255
00:58:33.200 --> 00:58:34.780
It's something he's always wanted.
这是他一直以来梦寐以求的。

1256
00:58:34.780 --> 00:58:36.380
For years he was looked over.
多年来他一直被人忽视。

1257
00:58:36.600 --> 00:58:38.160
I guess most kept getting it.
我猜大多数人一直在得奖。

1258
00:58:38.700 --> 00:58:40.420
He's super happy about it.
他对此高兴极了。

1259
00:58:40.540 --> 00:58:48.100
And there was a deleted scene between Angela and Dwight that I think was the nail in the coffin for her to really warm up to the senator.
安吉拉和德怀特之间还有一段被删减的戏，我认为那是她真正开始对参议员动心的临门一脚。

1260
00:58:48.100 --> 00:58:48.800
Oh.
哦。

1261
00:58:49.120 --> 00:58:49.640
Let's hear it.
说来听听。

1262
00:58:50.520 --> 00:58:51.040
Dwight.
德怀特。

1263
00:58:51.200 --> 00:58:51.800
It's time.
时间到了。

1264
00:58:52.260 --> 00:58:53.080
Um, sorry.
嗯，不好意思。

1265
00:58:53.200 --> 00:58:55.240
Women aren't allowed to address the Hay King directly.
女性不得直接向干草之王进言。

1266
00:58:55.440 --> 00:58:55.960
Go away.
走开。

1267
00:58:56.580 --> 00:58:56.960
It's okay.
没关系。

1268
00:58:58.860 --> 00:59:00.520
I've been waiting for you all day.
我等你一整天了。

1269
00:59:00.940 --> 00:59:01.700
What are you talking about?
你在说什么呢？

1270
00:59:02.640 --> 00:59:03.080
Right.
对。

1271
00:59:03.280 --> 00:59:03.640
The thing.
那件事。

1272
00:59:03.860 --> 00:59:03.980
Okay.
好吧。

1273
00:59:04.100 --> 00:59:07.120
Just get yourself ready and cleaned up and I'll meet you there when this winds down.
你赶紧收拾清洗一下，这里忙完了我在那儿跟你汇合。

1274
00:59:08.120 --> 00:59:09.060
Be gone, woman.
退下吧，女人。

1275
00:59:09.720 --> 00:59:10.240
Yeah.
对。

1276
00:59:10.520 --> 00:59:11.380
Be gone, woman.
退下吧，女人。

1277
00:59:11.600 --> 00:59:18.920
And while he says that, he's gnawing on a giant, like, turkey leg and wearing a fake crown made of straw.
他说这话的时候，正啃着一根巨大的像火鸡腿一样的东西，头上还戴着一顶稻草做的假王冠。

1278
00:59:19.340 --> 00:59:21.860
Well, I believe that was meant to be a goat leg.
哦，我觉得那本来应该是个山羊腿。

1279
00:59:22.140 --> 00:59:22.660
Oh.
哦。

1280
00:59:22.660 --> 00:59:24.220
Because remember the petting zoo?
因为还记得那个抚摸动物园吗？

1281
00:59:24.360 --> 00:59:26.280
Oh, it was roasting goats.
哦，那是烤山羊。

1282
00:59:26.280 --> 00:59:26.640
Yeah.
对。

1283
00:59:27.020 --> 00:59:29.040
It was closed right before the goat roaSt.
就在烤山羊活动开始前不久关门了。

1284
00:59:29.340 --> 00:59:29.520
Yeah.
对。

1285
00:59:30.080 --> 00:59:34.960
Alicia Raycraft, our costume designer, made the whole Hay King outfit.
艾丽西亚·雷克拉夫特，我们的服装设计师，制作了整套干草之王服装。

1286
00:59:35.140 --> 00:59:36.140
It's really great.
真的很棒。

1287
00:59:36.300 --> 00:59:38.640
She sent me some of the sketches when she was sketching it out.
她设计草图的时候发给我过一些。

1288
00:59:39.060 --> 00:59:40.100
It's pretty perfect.
简直完美。

1289
00:59:41.080 --> 00:59:45.680
Clearly, though, Dwight was always meant to win because that crown was never going on a child's head.
不过很显然，德怀特注定是要赢的，因为那顶王冠根本不可能戴在一个小孩子的头上。

1290
00:59:45.920 --> 00:59:46.160
No.
没错。

1291
00:59:46.740 --> 00:59:47.100
I mean.
我是说。

1292
00:59:47.400 --> 00:59:49.020
Rain has a huge head in real life.
雷恩现实中头超大。

1293
00:59:49.120 --> 00:59:50.100
And it fit him perfectly.
而且它戴在他头上正合适。

1294
00:59:50.480 --> 00:59:52.260
Kevin is still stuck in the maze.
凯文还困在迷宫里。

1295
00:59:52.940 --> 00:59:53.840
Poor Brian.
可怜的布莱恩。

1296
00:59:54.200 --> 00:59:55.400
Poor Brian this day.
今天可怜的布莱恩。

1297
00:59:55.640 --> 00:59:57.480
Running around 90 degrees.
在九十度的高温下奔跑。

1298
00:59:58.140 --> 00:59:59.100
Full sun.
烈日当空。

1299
00:59:59.580 --> 01:00:01.280
What we do for our craft.
为了艺术我们可真拼啊。

1300
01:00:01.440 --> 01:00:01.960
I know.
可不是嘛。

1301
01:00:02.360 --> 01:00:05.900
Well, you know, in the kitchen, Michael was not going to sell.
嗯，你知道的，在厨房里，迈克尔是不打算卖的。

1302
01:00:05.900 --> 01:00:13.620
He said he believed in Ryan, that he would give Ryan the full nine days to turn Woof around, and then they would sell.
他说他相信瑞安，他会给瑞安足足九天时间来扭转伍夫公司的局面，然后他们再卖掉。

1303
01:00:13.880 --> 01:00:14.960
It's kind of cool.
这挺酷的。

1304
01:00:15.120 --> 01:00:17.760
He says, you know, the world sends people your way.
他说，你知道的，世界会把各种人送到你身边。

1305
01:00:18.620 --> 01:00:23.960
Sometimes you don't know why, but he always sticks with his people.
有时你不知道为什么，但他总是对身边的人不离不弃。

1306
01:00:24.100 --> 01:00:25.360
Basically, I'm summing up.
基本上，我在做个总结。

1307
01:00:25.360 --> 01:00:33.060
And I actually thought it was very Michael, and he goes through and he kind of likens everybody to a playing card.
而且我真的觉得这很有迈克尔的风格，他通读了一遍，然后把每个人都比作扑克牌。

1308
01:00:33.420 --> 01:00:34.420
He's the Joker.
他是小丑牌。

1309
01:00:35.240 --> 01:00:35.800
Yes.
是的。

1310
01:00:35.800 --> 01:00:40.700
And it's true that Ryan is a two, but sometimes twos can be wild.
而且瑞安确实是张二，但有时候二可以当王牌用。

1311
01:00:41.260 --> 01:00:41.560
Yeah.
对。

1312
01:00:41.860 --> 01:00:42.140
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1313
01:00:42.860 --> 01:00:44.640
Michael really doesn't give up on people.
迈克尔真的不会放弃任何人。

1314
01:00:45.840 --> 01:00:47.820
But Ryan's going to give up on Woof.
但瑞安却要抛弃乌夫网了。

1315
01:00:48.200 --> 01:00:48.960
Thank God.
谢天谢地。

1316
01:00:48.960 --> 01:00:54.220
He spent about two hours in his closet, and the episode ends with Michael getting a final Woof.
他在衣帽间里待了大约两个小时，这一集以迈克尔收到最后一声“汪”结束。

1317
01:00:54.780 --> 01:00:55.420
Yes.
是的。

1318
01:00:55.780 --> 01:00:58.460
It said, Woof from Ryan Howard.
上面写着，来自瑞安·霍华德的汪。

1319
01:00:58.640 --> 01:01:00.000
Decided to sell company.
决定出售公司。

1320
01:01:00.260 --> 01:01:00.940
Thanks, bro.
谢啦，兄弟。

1321
01:01:01.220 --> 01:01:02.120
Hell of a ride.
真是一段刺激的旅程。

1322
01:01:02.440 --> 01:01:05.400
This was like a few days together.
这就像是相处了几天一样。

1323
01:01:06.420 --> 01:01:12.340
And one last thing we have to address is that the Hay King goes looking for Angela.
我们要解决的最后一件事是，草垛之王去找安吉拉了。

1324
01:01:12.780 --> 01:01:13.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1325
01:01:13.220 --> 01:01:20.760
And taped to the warehouse door where they hook up is a voided contract and the punch card.
贴在他们幽会的仓库门上的，是一份作废的合同和打卡纸。

1326
01:01:21.140 --> 01:01:29.840
And as Angela's leaving, the senator asks, if I were to call Dunder Mifflin and ask for Angela Martin, would I get through to you?
当安吉拉离开时，参议员问，如果我打电话给邓德米夫林找安吉拉·马丁，能找到你吗？

1327
01:01:29.960 --> 01:01:31.120
And she says, yes.
她说，能。

1328
01:01:31.380 --> 01:01:35.860
And if I were to call your home and ask for your wife, would I get her?
那如果我打你家电话找你妻子，能找到她吗？

1329
01:01:36.140 --> 01:01:38.500
And he says, no, my wife died.
他说，不能，我妻子去世了。

1330
01:01:38.940 --> 01:01:39.980
He's the widower.
他是个鳏夫。

1331
01:01:40.220 --> 01:01:40.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1332
01:01:40.600 --> 01:01:43.680
We get a tiny smile from Angela on that one.
对于这一点，安吉拉露出了一个淡淡的微笑。

1333
01:01:44.120 --> 01:01:46.920
And that, my friends, was Woof.com.
朋友们，这就是 Woof.com。

1334
01:01:47.560 --> 01:01:50.260
Thank you so much for sending in your questions.
非常感谢大家发来问题。

1335
01:01:50.540 --> 01:01:54.440
Thank you so much to Erin Schur for stopping by and letting us chat his ear off.
非常感谢埃林·舒尔抽空做客，让我们拉着他聊个不停。

1336
01:01:54.620 --> 01:01:57.400
Thank you to Randy Cordray for all your behind-the-scenes info.
感谢兰迪·科德雷提供所有的幕后信息。

1337
01:01:57.400 --> 01:02:00.140
And Ainsley, thanks for that breakdown on Hay vs. Straw.
还有英斯利，谢谢你为我们剖析干草与麦秸的区别。

1338
01:02:00.460 --> 01:02:01.420
All right, you guys.
好了，各位。

1339
01:02:01.420 --> 01:02:03.280
Have a great one from two Office Ladies.
来自两位办公室女士的祝福，祝你们过得愉快。

1340
01:02:03.580 --> 01:02:04.640
We wish you the beSt.
祝你们一切都好。

1341
01:02:04.920 --> 01:02:05.700
See you soon.
回头见。

1342
01:02:05.900 --> 01:02:13.590
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1343
